{"skill":{"slug":"sonoscli","displayName":"Sonoscli"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545381030,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":940,"sha256":"0b9cf84b375cd2269aa7c295a776129c3c630b916ea66f9fd0b49feb76ba7499","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1874,"sha256":"9cb1b7e281822a20a2199f593a0e4a79c004cff9cd6b3b867cfbbe45535c80a7","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013623569,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b1310f36a3629dc77c67e415fbfa123bf5c37433e1a963da50597a3f2eeac13c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b1310f36a3629dc77c67e415fbfa123bf5c37433e1a963da50597a3f2eeac13c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: sonoscli\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It installs the `sonoscli` tool from a public Go module (`github.com/steipete/sonoscli`) and provides instructions for controlling Sonos speakers. The `SKILL.md` mentions the optional requirement for `SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID/SECRET` environment variables for Spotify search functionality, which is a standard practice for API integrations and does not indicate any attempt at credential exfiltration or prompt injection against the agent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159626294},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789013623569},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Sonos control helper, with the main caution that it installs an unpinned third-party Go CLI.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Local-network Sonos access and optional Spotify API environment variables are proportionate to the advertised speaker-control and search features.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation uses github.com/steipete/sonoscli/cmd/sonos@latest, which is disclosed and purpose-aligned but mutable, so future installs may resolve to code different from what was reviewed.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The runtime instructions are direct examples for using the sonos command and do not contain prompt hijacking, hidden role changes, broad file access, or unrelated agent behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact does not request background services, scheduled tasks, persistent memory changes, privilege escalation, or modification of agent tools.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is controlling Sonos speakers, and the documented commands are limited to discovery, status, playback, volume, grouping, favorites, queue actions, and optional Spotify search.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, consider that the CLI is fetched from a third-party Go module using @latest. Install only if you trust that upstream project, and avoid exposing unrelated secrets in the environment when running it.","findings":"[T08] expected: The unpinned remote Go dependency is a real supply-chain caution, but the dependency is openly declared, matches the Sonos CLI purpose, and there is no artifact evidence of malicious or deceptive behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013623569}}}}}